        "title": "Literary Modernism - Joyce, Woolf, Proust, Kafka, Mann, Musil",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Literary modernism is not a style — it is a response to a crisis of representation. The realist novel had worked by assuming: there is a stable external world; it can be described accurately; language is adequate to that description; and a narrating consciousness can observe it reliably."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-MODERNISM.md#003",
