        "title": "Literary Modernism - Joyce, Woolf, Proust, Kafka, Mann, Musil",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RELIABLE LANGUAGE:\n  ─ Words don't point to stable things.\n  ─ Language is layered, ambiguous, historically conditioned.\n  ─ (Saussure's linguistics: signs are arbitrary; meaning is relational)"
    },
