        "title": "Literary Modernism - Joyce, Woolf, Proust, Kafka, Mann, Musil",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE STABLE SELF:\n  ─ There is no unified consistent \"I\" — consciousness is a stream,\n    not a container.\n  ─ The self is constituted by time, memory, language, and desire.\n  ─ (Freud; Bergson on time; James on the stream of consciousness)"
    },
